  "description": "Weird random run because exploring new trails is the only way for me to get away from my demons. Had vague notions of getting to Alta mountain but it was a bit rugged and far for that with weather not trending in a good direction, so I turned around at a random overlook of Hibox. I was looking for the Lake Laura waterfall in dense bushwhack when I heard a chirp that I'm 80-85% sure was a mountain lion. There were no birds around and I was way off trail by a water source. When I heard it the second time I turned tail and gtfo'd. My watch died on the way back so I spliced in a phone recording from when I looked down and noticed.",
